# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A widget body carries inline wikitext on its own line"

# TiddlyWiki parses a widget's content as wikitext, so a transclusion, a link, bold
# and a macro call read inside a one-line widget body as they read in a sentence.

<$button>{{Some/Tiddler}}</$button>
#        ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.widget.button.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.transclusion.transcludeinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.transclusion.transcludeinline.begin.tiddlywiki5

<$button>[[Some Target]]</$button>
#          ^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.widget.button.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.tiddlywiki5

<$button>''strong''</$button>
#          ^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.widget.button.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.bold.tiddlywiki5

<$button class=x><<myMacro one>></$button>
#                  ^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.widget.button.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
